package views

// The brand mark: an engraved portrait of an anthropomorphic Victorian duck
// gentleman (top hat, monocle, tweed three-piece), a nod to Dagobert Duck.
// Used in the rail at 32px, in empty states at 96-112px, and on the sign-in
// page, which has no rail for it to sit in.

// medallion sets the portrait in a circular disc with a seal-green ring. The
// artwork is framed so the head and collar fill the disc and the body falls
// outside it; a full-length figure shrinks to an illegible speck at 32px.
//
// mark.webp has its cream paper composited in rather than relying on
// mix-blend-mode over whatever sits behind it, so it renders identically on
// both themes — inverting an engraving turns the top hat white, at which point
// it stops being a portrait.
//
// Raster, not vector: the engraving has no vector original, and its hatching
// would trace to something far larger than these 18 kB. Stored at 320px for a
// mark shown at 32px and 96-112px.
templ medallion(class string) {
	<img src="/public/assets/mark.webp" alt="" width="320" height="320" class={ "medallion " + class }/>
}

// rule — a plain hairline separator.
templ rule(class string) {
	<hr class={ "border-0 border-t hairline " + class }/>
}
